{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point","id":1100216,"title":"[2E] Voluntarily Fail a Breaking Point?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-04T14:27:52-07:00","id":1100216,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [2E] Voluntarily Fail a Breaking Point?","content":"As a player, can I choose to fail a Breaking Point to make progress towards Harmony 5?<br /> <br /> Cheers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/485-kal","name":"Kal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T15:53:17-07:00","id":1100234,"title":"","content":"Not by the rules as written. Your ST might allow it, but it sort of takes away some of the drama. Plus, Harmony 5 is explicitly the best place to be mechanically, and I'd argue it would allow one to game the system a bit too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T16:51:08-07:00","id":1100260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100234#post1100234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not by the rules as written. Your ST might allow it, but it sort of takes away some of the drama. Plus, Harmony 5 is explicitly the best place to be mechanically, and I'd argue it would allow one to game the system a bit too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it kind of takes some of the weight out of higher-Primal Urge werewolves destabilizing more easily* if you don't have to deliberately hamstring your Resolve or Composure or go to further lengths to fail your way towards the middle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Siskur-Dah and Essence hunger do a <i>lot</i> of heavy lifting on the Harmony scale - who knew?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T17:21:31-07:00","id":1100272,"title":"","content":"Yeah it kind of removes any teeth from Harmony if you can voluntarily fail Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T19:23:51-07:00","id":1100294,"title":"","content":"From a similar out of character standpoint you could just repeat the sin until your Harmony breaks the way you want it to, but in-character there's likely to be consequences for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T09:07:19-07:00","id":1100464,"title":"","content":"I was going to comment on how its a little weird that it is so hard to deliberately change your harmony considering that it is something that would be pretty important for the &quot;onboarding&quot; process of a new uratha, but on a re-read I found a surefire way to do it that I had forgotten about<b></b>: losing your physical touchstone shifts you towards spirit no matter what. I actually <b><i>really</i></b> like how this reinforces a lot of tropes that I like in a way that is so much better than fiddling with how breaking points towards harmony work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T09:19:35-07:00","id":1100467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100464#post1100464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to comment on how its a little weird that it is so hard to deliberately change your harmony considering that it is something that would be pretty important for the &quot;onboarding&quot; process of a new uratha,</div> </div> </div> </div>Harmony's meant to be tested a lot during play. You shouldn't have a problem just rolling and chancing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:07:52-07:00","id":1100480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100467#post1100467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Harmony's meant to be tested a lot during play. You shouldn't have a problem just rolling and chancing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the matter of the mounting one-way penalties that make it easier and easier to fall towards the ends the further from the middle you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:40:32-07:00","id":1100495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point#post1100216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a player, can I choose to fail a Breaking Point to make progress towards Harmony 5?<br /> <br /> Cheers</div> </div> </div> </div>My general rule is that the player can voluntarily fail any tests so long as the character is conscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T13:28:39-07:00","id":1100552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100467#post1100467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Harmony's meant to be tested a lot during play. You shouldn't have a problem just rolling and chancing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that the examples given are mostly guidelines, but the fact that some of them are so extreme (murder, cannibalism) leaves me uncertain what should count. It would make sense and make things simpler if the major steps of initiation into the Forsaken culture (swearing the Oath of the Moon, joining or forming a pack, getting a totem) were breaking points towards spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T13:33:32-07:00","id":1100555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100552#post1100552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that the examples given are mostly guidelines, but the fact that some of them are so extreme (murder, cannibalism) leaves me uncertain what should count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Murder's likely to pop up a lot, and cannibalism is on the table whenever someone rages, or just needs Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would make sense and make things simpler if the major steps of initiation into the Forsaken culture (swearing the Oath of the Moon, joining or forming a pack, getting a totem) were breaking points towards spirit. </div> </div> </div>Some of these things are likely to happen once in the life of a werewolf, for some characters like ghost wolves never. Besides, they're part of the character creation process so already tied into why you start with 7 when you have 9 after the First Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:11:48-07:00","id":1100577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100555#post1100555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of these things are likely to happen once in the life of a werewolf, for some characters like ghost wolves never. Besides, they're part of the character creation process so already tied into why you start with 7 when you have 9 after the First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I totally get that. This mostly just musing about what might have gone on between somebody's first change and when play starts to cause them to be at 7 when play starts, and how werewolf society would actively encourage newly changed wolves to do things to bring their harmony in balance and what those things might be. If all of the normal initiation type stuff is what actually contributes towards balancing your harmony during the first phase of your werewolfitude then a tiny part of me that has been going &quot;hmmm&quot; starts going &quot;ahhhh&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T00:56:27-07:00","id":1100747,"title":"","content":"Player risen in Harmony to 8 in previous sessions. To lower it, he wanted to commit murder. I run intense scene of his sacrificing innocent. I then pass rolling Resolve + Composure as player wanted to lower Harmony, and rolling will be anticlimactic with going for success, for player and my investment in the scene. Still, most of the time I would ask player to roll on his Harmony Breaking Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-06-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T04:52:36-07:00","id":1100776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100747#post1100747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player risen in Harmony to 8 in previous sessions. To lower it, he wanted to commit murder. I run intense scene of his sacrificing innocent. I then pass rolling Resolve + Composure as player wanted to lower Harmony, and rolling will be anticlimactic with going for success, for player and my investment in the scene. Still, most of the time I would ask player to roll on his Harmony Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, roll for them and fudge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T10:24:59-07:00","id":1100878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point#post1100216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a player, can I choose to fail a Breaking Point to make progress towards Harmony 5?<br /> Cheers</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it, intentionally failing this kind of roll is pushing a player desire onto a character's role-play. It's like the old alignment issues of D&amp;D: you've been doing a bunch of good deeds, and you're at risk of losing your neutral alignment, so you go and stab some random people and kick some puppies while you're at it. It can come off as reckless playing, or as if the player doesn't want to deal with the consequences of their actions and wants an easy out. There's definitely some in-game level of awareness of the Harmony mechanic, but I like to look at it more like what's pushing and pulling at the character's being, instincts, etc. instead of just a number and a roll. So if I were the ST, I'd say you can't just opt to fail the roll, but I'd also try to work with you as a player to find some in-character opportunities to balance things back out if that's what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T06:32:32-07:00","id":1101198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1100878#post1100878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I see it, intentionally failing this kind of roll is pushing a player desire onto a character's role-play. It's like the old alignment issues of D&amp;D: you've been doing a bunch of good deeds, and you're at risk of losing your neutral alignment, so you go and stab some random people and kick some puppies while you're at it. It can come off as reckless playing, or as if the player doesn't want to deal with the consequences of their actions and wants an easy out. There's definitely some in-game level of awareness of the Harmony mechanic, but I like to look at it more like what's pushing and pulling at the character's being, instincts, etc. instead of just a number and a roll. So if I were the ST, I'd say you can't just opt to fail the roll, but I'd also try to work with you as a player to find some in-character opportunities to balance things back out if that's what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: in character motivations are aspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T09:06:34-07:00","id":1101259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1101198#post1101198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re: in character motivations are aspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or out of character goals the player has for the character. Nor if what you were saying is true that excludes other mechanics also governing character motivation: example Blood and Bone, Harmony, Aspirations, Doors open against a character, and various merits all chip in with some weight on the matter.<br /> <br /> Aspiration Example:<br /> Fail at defending my mother from the Pure Packs harassing our kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-07-2017, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T02:07:22-07:00","id":1101535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1101259#post1101259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or out of character goals the player has for the character. Nor if what you were saying is true that excludes other mechanics also governing character motivation: example Blood and Bone, Harmony, Aspirations, Doors open against a character, and various merits all chip in with some weight on the matter.<br /> <br /> Aspiration Example:<br /> Fail at defending my mother from the Pure Packs harassing our kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes, I was the one who first stated that aspirations could be negative outcome like that back in that thread about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:32:51-07:00","id":1104083,"title":"","content":"The way is written is weird. This one case of applying the same mechanic to everything and not thinking things through.<br /> <br /> Normally in all the other WoD lines, when a players wants to fail a degeneration roll you let him because its rare the player who consciously shoot himself on the foot that way.<br /> <br /> However as it is now its a weird scenario, as falling a roll is actually good sometimes and passing a roll is bad in other times which leaves a bad taste in players mouth as it feels weird.<br /> <br /> The way i handle it now is the following. Every time you roll for harmony and you pass, you get a positive outcome and every time you fail one you get the negative one. So if your PC commits an act to make himself fall toward spirit and rolls a success and he is above 5 then he moves downward. Same situation but he is 5 or less and he succeed then he stays where he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-16-2017, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T14:42:51-07:00","id":1104485,"title":"","content":"I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\">resolve this issue</a> by having a 0-5 Spirit Harmony and 0-5 Flesh Harmony which totals to a 0-10 Harmony system when they add together, where &quot;high harmony&quot; representing having more in each sub stat.0-0 mean no Harmony towards flesh nor spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-16-2017, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T15:27:28-07:00","id":1104502,"title":"","content":"You could also amend it by altering the definitions of 'failure'. Any time you make a sin that would move you closer to 5, a 'failure' keeps you where you are - and a success moves you closer to the ideal harmony. Any time you make a sin that would move you away from 5, a failure moves you away and a success keeps you where you are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:04:44-07:00","id":1104515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1104485#post1104485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\">resolve this issue</a> by having a 0-5 Spirit Harmony and 0-5 Flesh Harmony which totals to a 0-10 Harmony system when they add together, where &quot;high harmony&quot; representing having more in each sub stat.0-0 mean no Harmony towards flesh nor spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did you deal with the affects of Harmony on shapeshifting? Or Death Rage Triggers? Or the Code of Honor Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T17:45:06-07:00","id":1105232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1100216-2e-voluntarily-fail-a-breaking-point?p=1104515#post1104515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How did you deal with the affects of Harmony on shapeshifting? Or Death Rage Triggers? Or the Code of Honor Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is for the shapeshifting and movement to the material or the hisil,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Alternate Harmony where &amp;quot;High Harmony&amp;quot; stat means having more Harmony between spirit and flesh</span></b><br /> Uratha are drawn back and forth between their role as apex spirit predator maintaining the balance of the spirit ecology and as beings of flesh in need of human connections. For an Uratha being pulled away from the spirit world is as dangerous to their emotional and mental well being as slipping away from the mundane normal world. To reflect the complex pull towards two different aspects of their nature, which is how Harmony is expressed, Uratha have two types of Supports. These Supports are capped at 5 each, for a total of 10. The first type is Human Supports which are the same as other supernaturals and mortals. The other type of Support is Spirit Supports which represents minor gaffling spirits within their territory which are evident of the spiritual health of aspects their territory. Think of these spirits as ecological indicator species found in the natural world. Like indicator species in the natural world the presence of these low level and often bottom of the food chain spirits show what the environmental factors foster. If these spirits are overfed and progress beyond gaffling shows imbalance, or if they are lost through through hurt, exposure, or vengeance they also indicate damage to the ecology. In these cases the damage represents neglect or abuse by the Uratha (Hurt), over exploitation or deliberate outside sabotage (Exposure) or reckless damage caused by reactionary rampage (Vengeance). Watching over, interacting with and keeping these spirits in line is the spiritual equivalent for a Uratha as maintaining their relationship with their territory. Uratha instinctively feel maintaining the status qua or equilibrium with these spirits keeps their territories, and thus their lives in balance, and they are correct that is a major factor in doing so.<br /> <br /> Uratha begin play with 4 Human Supports and 3 Spirit Supports. After their first change some human relationships fall away, and a new spiritual awareness awakens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Human Relationships</b><br /> Parent<br /> Sibling<br /> Child<br /> Lover<br /> Rival<br /> Mentor<br /> Protege<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Relationships</b><br /> Virtue<br /> Vice<br /> Artifical<br /> Nature<br /> Elemental<br /> Magath<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Spirit Supports<br /> At 4 or more Spirit Supports they don't need to roll to enter the Hisil.<br /> -1 to Rolls to enter the Material each.<br /> At 1 or less Spirit Supports takes the Primal Urge in Lethal wounds when changing forms.<br /> At 0 Spirit Supports the Uratha loses the ability to reach to the Hisil<br /> <br /> Human Support<br /> At 4 or more Human Supports they don't need to roll to enter the Material<br /> -1 to Rolls to enter the Hisil each.<br /> At 1 or less Human Supports treats all Banes as if had 1 Permanent Atrocity higher.<br /> At 0 Human Supports the Uratha loses the ability to reach to the Material.</div> </div> </div> </div>It includes the Atrocity and Support mechanics, and I need to copy paste my post about death rage, which take a moment to add as an exit to this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}